#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0397 expect=noViolation domain=FX
#note "THE DISCRIMINATING CASE OF SHEET ISSUE #128 (M3-D25, Fix #310) - the record that fired before the move and must not now. An UNREMARKABLE fetal-pathology finding with a BLANK FXSTAT, FXRESCAT empty. Sheet rows 1914-1915's Condition cell reads FXSTRESC ^= \"UNREMARKABLE\" OR FXSTAT ^= \"NOT DONE\"; the exemption in the SAME rows' Plain Text and Cited Guidance is a DISJUNCTION, so by De Morgan the rule applies only when BOTH inequalities hold - an AND. Written with OR, the first disjunct was false but the second was true (a blank FXSTAT is the normal state of a test that WAS done), so the Condition was satisfied and FXRESCAT was demanded on exactly the record the guidance exempts; the OR form made the exemption effectively unreachable. The Check now deliberately deviates from the Condition cell in favour of the same rows' Plain Text and Cited Guidance; Source stays verbatim, so the file disagrees with itself by design. Row 2 repeats the shape on a second subject."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
dataset FX class=FINDINGS label="Fetal Pathology Findings"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col FXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col FXTESTCD type=Char label="Fetal Pathology Test Short Name"
col FXSTRESC type=Char label="Character Result/Finding in Std Format"
col FXSTAT   type=Char label="Completion Status"
col FXRESCAT type=Char label="Result Category"
---
S1 | FX | 001 | 1 | FPEXAM | UNREMARKABLE |  | 
S1 | FX | 002 | 1 | FPEXAM | UNREMARKABLE |  | 
